# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Dungeon Grid Arena
# =============================================================================

# ---- Archived / internal-only documents -------------------------------------
# These were the early-stage spec drafts that the published Final Report and
# Summary Report supersede. Kept on disk for personal reference only.
docs/archive/

# ---- Kiro IDE workspace metadata --------------------------------------------
# Personal IDE state; not part of the code.
.kiro/

# ---- Build outputs ----------------------------------------------------------
# The graded submission ships prebuilt binaries; the repository tracks source
# only. Reviewers run the documented compile commands themselves.
*.exe
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.idb

# ---- The build artefacts of THIS project (explicit, in case the patterns
#       above are ever loosened) -------------------------------------------------
game.exe
game_raylib.exe
test_runner.exe

# ---- Vendored Raylib runtime DLL (the .a + headers are tracked) -------------
# raylib.dll is a 64-bit Windows binary; the test runner does not need it
# and reviewers can fetch it from the upstream Raylib release. Re-add this
# file by hand when packaging the submission ZIP if needed.
libs/raylib/lib/raylib.dll

# ---- CMake build trees ------------------------------------------------------
build/
out/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
CTestTestfile.cmake

# ---- Editor / OS junk -------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Python helpers / FFmpeg side install -----------------------------------
# imageio-ffmpeg lives in the user's AppData, but this rule guards against a
# venv ever being created inside the project root.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ---- Runtime data the player generates --------------------------------------
# These files are written by the game itself when the player saves or dies;
# they should never be tracked. The directory itself is preserved by the
# .gitkeep file we DO track.
data/savegame.txt
data/highscores.txt

# ---- Source video files no longer needed ------------------------------------
# The OGG audio tracks under assets/ are extracted from these MP4 sources
# once and committed; the source MP4s are gitignored to keep the repo small.
*.mp4
!test_cases_evidence/GameDemonstrationVideo.mp4

# Logs / scratch
*.log
scratch/
